.SH TYPE DEFINITIONS
The following simple, enumerated, and structure data types are defined 
in the 
.B am.h 
header file.
.PP
.ti 2
.BR SIMPLE
.Ty
AMF_DONE 
Media file state which indicates that 1 file has been fully processed.
.Ty
AMF_ERROR
Media file state which indicates that there is something wrong with a
file.
.Ty
AMF_RETRIEVED
Media file state which indicates that a file has been retrieved, and is
ready for processing.
.Ty
AMF_UNAVAILABLE
Media file state which indicates that a file is no longer available.
.Ty
AMF_UNPROCESSED
Media file state which indicates that no processing has begun on a
file.
.Ty
AMM_CREATING
Media state which indicates that a media request is being created.
.Ty
AMM_DONE
Media state which indicates that a media request have been fully
processed.
.Ty
AMM_ERROR
Media state which indicates that a media request has encountered
an error during processing.
.Ty
AMM_IN_PROG
Media state which indicates that a media request is currently 
being processed.
.Ty
AMU_CLEANED_UP
Media unit state which indicates that the unit has been cleaned up.
.Ty
AMU_DONE
Media unit state which indicates that the unit has been fully processed.
.Ty
AMU_PREPARED
Media unit state which indicates that the unit has been prepared.
.Ty
AMU_QUEUED
Media unit state which indicates that the unit has been queued.
.Ty
AMU_QUEUEING
Media unit state which indicates that the unit is being queued.
.Ty
AMU_WRITTEN
Media unit state which indicates that all copies of the unit have been 
written.
.Ty
AM_DEVICE_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a device character string.
.Ty
AM_DRIVER_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a device driver request name character string.
.Ty
AM_DEV_INFO_LEN
This is the maximum length of a device information character string.
.Ty
AM_FILE_ID_LEN
This is the maximum length of a file identifier character string.
.Ty
AM_FILE_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a file name character string.
.Ty
AM_LOGICAL_DEV_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a logical device name character string.
.Ty
AM_MEDIA_REQUEST_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a media request name character string.
.Ty
AM_MEDIA_REQUEST_TYPE_LEN
This is the maximum length of a media request type character string.
.Ty
AM_MEDIA_TYPE_LEN
This is the maximum length of a media type character string.
.Ty
AM_MEDIA_UNIT_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a media unit name character string.
.Ty
AM_MSTAGE_DIR_LEN
This is the maximum length of a staging directory character string.
.Ty
AM_PROC_NAME_LEN
This is the maximum length of a procedure name character string.
.Ty
AM_RT_ARCHIVE
Defines the media request archive type.
.Ty
AM_RT_USER
Defines the media request user type.
.Ty
AM_SOURCE_ID_LEN
This is the maximum length of a source identifier character string.
.Ty
AM_STATUS_SHORT_LEN
This is the maximum length of a short status message.
.Ty
AM_UNIT_NAME_ROOT_LEN
This is the maximum length of a media unit name root character string.

.PP
.ti 2
.BR ENUMERATED
.Ty
AM_DEVICE_CLEAR
An enumerated type used to indicate whether a device, a logical device,
or all devices should be cleared; made available.
The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_DC_ALL	/\(** All devices.	\(**/
AM_DC_LOGICAL	/\(** Matching a logical device name.	\(**/
AM_DC_DEVICE	/\(** Matching a given device name.	\(**/
.Ty
AM_DEVICE_GET
An enumerated type used to indicate the type of search that is to
be performed on the database for devices.  The members of this type 
are:
.Td/\(**
AM_DG_ALL	/\(** All devices.	\(**/
AM_DG_NAME	/\(** Match given device name.	\(**/
AM_DG_NAME_TYPE	/\(** Match given device name and	\(**/ 
	/\(** media type.	\(**/
AM_DG_NEXT	/\(** Next device, if  more than one.	\(**/
AM_DG_TYPE	/\(** Match given media type.	\(**/
.Ty
AM_FILE_GET 
An enumerated type to indicate which type of 'get' query to submit on the 
database's media_files table.  The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_FG_FILE_ID	/\(** Match given file ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_MEDIA_ID_FNAME	/\(** Match given file name.	\(**/
AM_FG_FNAME	/\(** Match given file name.	\(**/
AM_FG_MEDIA_FILE	/\(** Match given media request	\(**/
	/\(** and file IDs. \(**/
AM_FG_MEDIA_REQUEST_ID	
	/\(** Match given media request ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_MEDIA_UNIT	/\(** Match given media unit name	\(**/
	/\(** and media request ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_MEDIA_UNIT	/\(** Match given media unit.	\(**/
AM_FG_MEDIA_UNIT_ID	/\(** Match given media unit name and	\(**/
	/\(** and media request ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_NEXT	/\(** Next file, if more than one.	\(**/
AM_FG_QUEUEABLE	/\(** All files ready for queuing and	\(**/
	/\(** matching a request ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_RETRIEVABLE	/\(** All files need retrieving and	\(**/
	/\(** matching a request ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_SOURCE_ID	/\(** Match given source ID.	\(**/
AM_FG_STATUS	/\(** Match given status value.	\(**/
AM_FG_UNIT_FNAME	/\(** Match given media unit name, 	\(**/
	/\(** request ID, and file name.	\(**/
AM_FG_UNWRITTEN	/\(** Match a given request ID and 	\(**/
	/\(** have not been written.	\(**/
.Ty
AM_FILE_UPDATE 
An enumerated type to indicate which type of 'update' query to submit on the 
database's media_files table.  The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_FU_COMPLETE_ARCH	
	/\(** Set archive request to `done'.	\(**/
AM_FU_COMPLETE_USER	
	/\(** Set user request to `done'.	\(**/
AM_FU_MEDIA_Q_ROLLBACK	
	/\(** Dequeue a file from media unit.	\(**/
AM_FU_WRITTEN	/\(** Mark file as written
.Ty
AM_MEDIA_GET 
An enumerated type to indicate which type of 'get' query to submit on the 
database's media table. The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_MG_ALL	/\(** All media.	\(**/
AM_MG_MEDIA_REQUEST_ID	
	/\(** Match given request ID.	\(**/
AM_MG_MEDIA_REQUEST_NAME	
	/\(** Match given request name.	\(**/
AM_MG_NOTIFIABLE	/\(** All `notifiable' media.	\(**/
AM_MG_NEXT	/\(** Next media, if more than one.	\(**/
AM_MG_SOURCE_ID	/\(** Media with given source.	\(**/
AM_MG_STATUS	/\(** Media with given status.	\(**/
.Ty 
AM_SCRIPT_TYPE
An enumerated type used to indicate whether the script information for
preparing or writing is desired.  The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_ST_PREP	/\(** Get script details for prep script.	\(**/
AM_ST_WRITE	/\(** Get script details for write script.	\(**/
.Ty
AM_STAGE_GET
An enumerated type which is used to indicate what information is used to
query the database when `getting' information on media staging 
directories.  The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_SG_ALL	/\(** All staging directories.	\(**/
AM_SG_DIRECTORY	/\(** Match given staging directory.	\(**/
AM_SG_NEXT	/\(** Next staging directory.	\(**/
AM_SG_REQUEST_ID_NAME	
	/\(** Match given media request ID	\(**/
	/\(** and unit name.	\(**/
.Ty
AM_TYPE_GET
An enumerated type which is used to indicate/specify the type of database
query performed when `getting' media type information. The members of this
type are:
.Td
AM_TG_ALL	/\(** All media types
AM_TG_NEXT	/\(** Next media type, if more than one
AM_TG_TYPE	/\(** Match a given media type
.Ty
AM_UNIT_GET 
An enumerated type to indicate which type of 'get' query to submit on the 
database's media_units table.  The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_UG_MEDIA_REQUEST_ID	
	/\(** Match given media request ID.	\(**/
AM_UG_MEDIA_REQUEST_ID_LAST	
	/\(** Last media unit that matches	\(**/
	/\(** given request ID.	\(**/
AM_UG_MEDIA_REQUEST_ID_NAME
	/\(** Match given media request ID	\(**/
	/\(** and unit name.	\(**/
AM_UG_MEDIA_UNIT_NAME	/\(** Match given media unit name	\(**/
AM_UG_NEXT	/\(** Next unit, if more than one.	\(**/
AM_UG_NOTIFIABLE 	/\(** Determine if unit is cleaned up.	\(**/
AM_UG_STATUS	/\(** Match a given status value.	\(**/
AM_UG_STATUS_AFTER_NAME	
	/\(** Units after a given media unit	\(**/
	/\(** that match  given media ID and.	\(**/
	/\(** status value.	\(**/
.Ty
AM_UNIT_UPDATE 
An enumerated type to indicate which type of 'update' query to submit on the 
database's media_units table.  The members of this type are:
.Td
AM_UU_COMPLETE_USER	/\(** Set user media request as complete.	\(**/
.PP
.ti 2
.BR STRUCTURE
.Ty
AM_DEVICE
A structure containing information which describes a device which may
be used to create physical medium.  The information includes
whether or not the device is busy.  The members of the structure are:
.Ss
char	amdDeviceName[AM_DEVICE_NAME_LEN];
		/\(** Device name.	\(*\(**/
char	amdDeviceDriver[AM_DRIVER_NAME_LEN];
		/\(/\(** Device driver.	\(*\(**/
char	amdDeviceInfo[AM_DEV_INFO_LEN];
		/\(** Device information.	\(*\(**/
char	amdType[AM_MEDIA_TYPE_LEN];
		/\(** Type of device.	\(*\(**/
int	amdRSpeed;	/\(** Read speed.	\(*\(**/
int	amdWSpeed;	/\(** Write speed.	\(*\(**/
boolean	amdOnline;	/\(** TRUE if device is on-line.	\(*\(**/
boolean	amdInUse;	/\(** TRUE means in use.	\(*\(**/
pid_t	amdProcessId;	/\(** Process ID using device.	\(*\(**/
char	amdProcessName[AM_PROC_NAME_LEN];
		/\(** Name of process using dev.	\(*\(**/
int	amdMediaRequestId;
		/\(** Media request ID.	\(*\(**/
char	amdMediaUnitName[AM_MEDIA_UNIT_NAME_LEN];
		/\(** Media unit name.	\(*\(**/
 time_t	amdTimeStamp;	/\(** Time when booked.	\(*\(**/
.Ty
AM_FILE
A structure containing information pertinent to a file in
the Media Archive database tables for the purposes of being written 
to physical medium. The members of the structure are:
.Ss
boolean	amfCompressionFlag;	
