.SH DESCRIPTION
The am library provides an interface to the Archive Media database 
and configurable parameters. The intended use for the Archive Media 
database and library (AM) is to aid in the creation of physical media.

The library has its own configuration file,
.I libam.config,
which contains all required configuration information.

The various library functions are briefly described below:
.Ty
amActionAdd()
This function adds an action to the 
.B media_actions
table. The action should
be one of: AM_MA_INGEST, AM_MA_UNINGEST, AM_MA_QUEUE, AM_MA_UNQUEUE, 
AM_MA_PREPARE, AM_MA_UNPREPARE, AM_MA_WRITE, AM_MA_UNWRITE, AM_MA_CLEANUP,
or AM_MA_UNCLEANUP. The media unit name may be null.
.Ty
amActionDelete()
This function removes all actions associated with the media request id and
media unit name from the 
.B media_actions 
table. The media unit name may be null.
.Ty
amAmountOnUnit()
Determine the number of kilobytes of data on a given media unit.
.Ty
amAmountQueueable()
Determine the number of kilobytes of data that is ready for queuing
for a particular media request.
.Ty
amAmountRetrievable()
Determine the number of kilobytes of data that is ready for retrieval 
for a particular media request.
.Ty
amCleanedUp()
Determine if a media unit has been cleaned up.
.Ty
amClose()
Free up local 
.B am 
structures and close the library.
.Ty
amDataStageGet()
Fetch the configured paths to the 
.B am 
data stage directories; user data stage, archive data stage,
and media data stage.
.Ty
amDbInfoGet()
Fetch information about the databases that 
.B am 
is using. 
.Ty
amDeviceBook()
Book a device, mark the device as busy, in the bookDevice table.
.Ty
amDeviceClear()
Free a device, mark the device as not busy, in the bookDevice table.
.Ty
amDeviceGet()
Fetch information describing a device(s). The information is composed
from the devices and bookDevice tables.
.Ty
amDeviceLookup()
Fetch all devices that are associated with a given logical device name.
The information is composed
from the devices and bookDevice tables.
.Ty
amFileDelete() 
Delete a file from the database's media_files table.
.Ty
amFileGet() 
Fetch information from the database's media_files table. 
.Ty
amFilePut()
Add information to the database's media_files table.
.Ty
amFileUpdate()
Update one or more tuples in the database's media_files table.
.Ty
amGet()
Fetch information from the database's media table. 
.Ty
amIngestGet()
Fetch the script name, from
.B am's
configuration file, which is to be used by
.B mediaIngest
for computing uncompressed file sizes.
.Ty
amInit()
Initialize the am library. Configuration and local structure allocation 
takes place in this routine. 
.Ty
amMediaIdGet()
Fetch a new media ID from the database's keys table. 
.Ty
amMedTypeGet()
Fetch information from the 
.B am's 
mediaTypes table which describes the various physical medium to 
be used.
.Ty
amMSBook()
Book a media staging area for the preparation of a physical media.  This
function alters the media stages table.
.Ty
amMSClear()
Release a media staging area which was used to prepare and write a physical 
media.  This function alters the media stages table.
.Ty
amMSGet()
Fetch information from the database's media_stages table. 
.Ty
amNotifiable()
Determine if a given media request is ready to notify its source that the
request has been completed.  An archive request is `notifiable' when there
is one or more media units which have been written and cleaned up.  An
user request is `notifiable' when all files have been written to a physical
media and all media units are cleaned up. 
.Ty
amNumCleanupable()
Determine the number of media units for a given media request that can be 
cleaned up, or those that have been written.
.Ty
amNumCopiesWritten()
Determine the number of copies of a given media unit that have been written
onto a physical medium.
.Ty
amNumOnUnit()
Determine the number files on a given media unit.
.Ty
amNumPreparable()
Determine the number of media units for a given media request that are ready
for preparation.
.Ty
amNumWriteable()
Determine the number of media units that are ready for writing.
.Ty
amPrecisionGet()
Fetch the default unit name precision value from
.B am's
configuration file.
.Ty
amPrepared()
Determine whether or not a given media unit has been prepared.
.Ty
amPut()
Add information to the database's media table.
.Ty
amScript()
Fetch the name of the write or prepare  script and configuration 
file to be used from 
.B am's
configuration file.
.Ty
amStatusStr()
Return a string which describes a valid am status. 
.Ty
amUnitDelete()
Remove information from the datbase's media_units table. 
.Ty
amUnitGet()
Fetch information from the database's media_units table. 
.Ty
amUnitPut()
Add information to the database's media_units table. 


.SH FILES
.SS libAm.config
The 
.B am 
library requires a configuration file which contains information 
about the Archive Media tables used by the library, and regarding data staging
areas on disk, and physical medium types.  The file should be named
.I libAm.config
and located in a directory specified by a 
.B CONFIG_DIR 
environment variable ( see the
.B ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
section )  The configuration file format is as follows:

.nf
.na
.ta 8n 16n 24n 32n 40n 48n 56n 64n 72n 80n 88n 96n 104n 112n 120n

#
#   Data Stage Paths.
#
# Keyword	User			Archive			Media
# --------	----			-------			-----
#

dataStage	/staging/storage/user	/staging/storage/archive /staging/media


#
#  Request database parameters
#
#  Keywd  database  database	media	media_files	media_units	media_stages	status	media_actions
#	  server    table	table		table	  	table		table
#  -----  --------  --------	-----	-----------	-----------	------------	------	-------------
#

amDb	  SYBASE	am	media	media_files	media_units	media_stages	status	media_actions




#
#  Request device table parameters
#
#  Keywd	device		booking		logicalDevice	mediaTypes
#		table		table		table		table
#  -----	-----------	--------	-------------	----------
#

deviceTables	devices		bookDevice	logicalDevices	mediaTypes



#
#   Media scripts.
#
# Keyword  Media Type	Prep Script		Prep Config. File    Write Script	    Write Config. File
#--------  -----------	------------		-----------------    ------------	    ------------------
#

scripts	  TP		none		     	none		    tpWrite		     none
scripts	  CD            cdPrepRunMkisofs-111	mkisofs-111.config  cdWriteRunCdrecord-16    none
scripts	  VD		dvdPrepRunMkisofs-111	mkisofs-111.config  dvdWriteRunCdrecord-16   none



#
#   mediaIngest script name (This line is optional in the config file.
#   It is the script name for determining the uncompressed size of a file)
#
# Keyword  	Script Name
#--------  	-----------
#

ingestScript	mi_size	


#
#   media unit names have a numerical value appended to the unit name root.
#   This number is padded with 0's; the number of 0's depends on the 
#   precision value.  The precision value is normally obtained from the
#   media table, however, in order to provide backwards compatibility the
#   default, defined here, is used if no value is given.
#
# Keyword  		precision
#--------  		-----------
#

defaultPrecision	4


.ad
.fi

